{
  "generated_description": "Crime in India compiles national-level crime statistics for India across 1953 to 2023, spanning 67 editions/periods. The series tracks key indicators such as cognizable crimes registered, IPC and Local & Special Law cases, and outcomes including disposal of cases and details on courts and period of trials. It also covers victim-based reporting for offences like murder, kidnapping & abduction, and rape, along with property stolen and recovered. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB), it supports trend analysis and policy and policing research.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Census 2001 statistics on institutional households, broken down by household size, for India at the national level. It supports analysis of how institutional living arrangements vary across household-size categories and can be used for demographic profiling and planning. The data are published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs, reflecting central census operations. The scope is limited to the Census 2001 reference year.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Motor Transport Statistics provides national-level time series on road transport and highway-related indicators across editions spanning 1970-71 to 2001-2002. It covers registered motor vehicles, road accidents (persons killed and injured), and licensing statistics such as valid driving and conductor licences. The catalog also includes physical and financial performance measures for State Road Transport Undertakings (SRTUs), along with revenue realised from road transport and information on national highway length. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways for monitoring and analysis of transport infrastructure and operations.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles Census-based counts of non-workers by main activity, age group, and sex for India at the national level, covering the Census editions 1991, 2001, and 2011. It captures non-worker categories such as students, household duties, dependents, retired persons/pensioners, rentiers, beggars, and vagrants, enabling analysis of demographic patterns by age and gender. Published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs, it supports research and planning focused on labour-force participation and population structure.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles state/UT-wise statistics on newly registered motor vehicles and the total number of registered motor vehicles. It covers both transport and non-transport categories, enabling analysis of vehicle fleet growth and composition by type. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, the data supports planning for road transport infrastructure, policy monitoring, and trend analysis across the road-vehicle ecosystem. The geographic coverage spans 35 States/UTs: Andhra Pradesh through West Bengal, and Andaman and Nicobar Islands through Puducherry. Temporal scope is not stated.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on solid waste management for the City of Chennai, Tamil Nadu, covering the end-to-end system from household-level source segregation to door-to-door (D2D) collection. It addresses bin placement and sizes, collection vehicle types and capacities, and the processing and disposal options for collected waste. The scope supports planning and monitoring of waste quantities and collection efficiency, with relevance to sanitation and urban service delivery under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and related Smart Cities Mission stakeholders.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Municipal Waste, Water and Sanitation; Sanitation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Union Budget editions covering 2018-19, 2021-22, 2022-23 and 2023-24 at the all-India (national) level. The catalog brings together annual financial statements presented by the Government of India, including budget estimates and revised figures for receipts and expenditures, along with key fiscal indicators such as revenue and capital allocations, deficit measures, and tax and subsidy-related components. Published by the Ministry of Finance and the Department of Economic Affairs, it supports analysis of central fiscal policy, budgeting trends, and allocation of resources across sectors.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Revenue"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Union Budget 2019-20 (Interim) catalog brings together budget documents and related indicators for India at the national level. It focuses on key fiscal themes such as receipts, expenditure, and deficit, supporting analysis of interim budget provisions and their implications for central finances. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, the catalog is intended for researchers, policymakers, and analysts who need consolidated budget information for the 2019-20 interim period.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Revenue"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Village/Town-wise Primary Census Abstract provides 2011 Census statistics at the village and town level for 34 States/UTs, supporting detailed demographic and socio-economic analysis. It covers key indicators such as households, population (including age group 0–6), SC/ST population, literacy and work participation, and worker categories including main and marginal workers with related occupational roles. The catalog is published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, and is useful for planning, research, and evidence-based policy across diverse geographies.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}
